## Instructions
Extract any of the following fields from the user message. Only return fields that are clearly mentioned — do NOT guess or assume. If a field is already set in the current spec and the user is not changing it, leave it as-is.

Fields to extract:
- source_system: The system data comes FROM (e.g., s4hana, wms, salesforce, demandware, afs, kafka, ems)
- target_system: The system data goes TO (e.g., kafka, afs, rest, ems, s4hana, demandware)
- business_object: The business entity or data object (e.g., article, invoice, order, stock, shipment, customer, price)
- interface_type: The integration pattern — MUST be one of: pub, sub, service
- template_type: The BWCE template name (e.g., REST_SERVICE_To_KAFKATopic, REST_PUB_To_KAFKATopic)
- cdm: Boolean, true if Common Data Model transformation is needed
- scenario_id: IKD Scenario ID (numeric, e.g., 1234)
- interface_id: IKD Interface ID (e.g., IKD-001)
- country_code: Country code (2-letter ISO, or NA if not applicable)
- unique_id: Unique identifier suffix (or NA if not applicable)
- env: Deployment environment (DEV, SIT, UAT, PROD, or comma-separated)
- email: Contact email address
- k8s_domain: Kubernetes namespace domain (e.g., cite)
- bitbucket_project: Bitbucket project name

## Interface Type Resolution
- pub/publish/producer/send/outbound → "pub"
- sub/subscribe/consumer/receive/listen/inbound → "sub"
- service/api/request-reply/sync/endpoint → "service"

## System Alias Resolution
- sap/s4/sapretail/sapr3 → "s4hana"
- sf/sfdc → "salesforce"
- dw/sfcc/commerce cloud → "demandware"
- jms → "ems"
- kafkatopic → "kafka"

## Response Format
Respond ONLY with valid JSON containing the extracted fields. Do not include fields you cannot determine. Do not include explanations.

Example response:
{
  "source_system": "s4hana",
  "target_system": "kafka",
  "business_object": "article",
  "interface_type": "pub",
  "cdm": false
}
